{
  "title": "66: al-Tahreem التحريم",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّبِىُّ لِمَ تُحَرِّمُ مَاۤ اَحَلَّ اللّٰهُ لَكَ‌ۚ تَبْتَغِىْ مَرْضَاتَ اَزْوَاجِكَ‌ؕ وَاللّٰهُ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(1)\nYAA AYYOHAL NABIYYO LEMA TUHARREMU MAA AAHALLA LAAHO LAKA TABTAGHEAA MARZAATA AAZWAAJEKA WAL LAAHO GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nO Prophet! Why holdest thou to be forbidden that which Allah has made lawful to thee? Thou seekest to please thy consorts. But Allah is Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful. \nقَدْ فَرَضَ اللّٰهُ لَكُمْ تَحِلَّةَ اَيْمَانِكُمْ‌ؕ وَاللّٰهُ مَوْلٰٮكُمْ‌ۚ وَهُوَ الْعَلِيْمُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(2)\nQAD FARAZA LAAHO LAKUM TAHELLATA AAYMAANEKUM WAL LAAHO MAWLAAKUM WA HOWA A’LEEM HAKEEM.\nAllah has already ordained for you, (O men), the dissolution of your oaths (in some cases): and Allah is your Protector, and He is Full of Knowledge and Wisdom. \nوَاِذْ اَسَرَّ النَّبِىُّ اِلٰى بَعْضِ اَزْوَاجِهٖ حَدِيْثًا‌ۚ فَلَمَّا نَبَّاَتْ بِهٖ وَاَظْهَرَهُ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ عَرَّفَ بَعْضَهٗ وَاَعْرَضَ عَنْۢ بَعْضٍ‌ۚ فَلَمَّا نَبَّاَهَا بِهٖ قَالَتْ مَنْ اَنْۢبَاَكَ هٰذَا‌ؕ قَالَ نَبَّاَنِىَ الْعَلِيْمُ الْخَبِیْرُ‏(3)\nWA IZ AASARRA NABIYYO ELAA BAA’ZE AAZWAAJEH HADEESAN FALAMMAA NABBAAT BEHI WAAZHARAHU LAAHO A’LAYHE A’ARRAFA BAA’ZAH WA A-A’RAZA A’N ELAA FALAMMAA NABBAAHAA BEHI QAALAT MAN AANBAAKA HAAZAA QAALA NABBAANEAAA A’LEEM KHABEER.\nWhen the Prophet disclosed a matter in confidence to one of his consorts, and she then divulged it (to another), and Allah made it known to him, he confirmed part thereof and repudiated a part. Then when he told her thereof, she said, “Who told thee this? “He said, “He told me Who knows and is well-acquainted (with all things).” \nاِنْ تَتُوْبَاۤ اِلَى اللّٰهِ فَقَدْ صَغَتْ قُلُوْبُكُمَا‌ۚ وَاِنْ تَظٰهَرَا عَلَيْهِ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ مَوْلٰٮهُ وَجِبْرِيْلُ وَصَالِحُ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‌ۚ وَالْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ بَعْدَ ذٰلِكَ ظَهِيْرٌ‏(4)\nIN TATOOBAA ELAL LAAHE FAQAD SAGHAT QULOOBUKUMAA WA TAZAAHARAA A’LAYHE FA-INNAL LAAHA HOWA MAWLAAHU WAJEBREELU WASAALEHU MOAMENEEN WAL MALAAA-EKATO BA’DA ZAALEKA ZAHEERUN.\nIf ye two turn in repentance to Him, your hearts are indeed so inclined; But if ye back up each other against him, truly Allah is his Protector, and Gabriel, and (every) righteous one among those who believe, and furthermore, the angels - will back (him) up. \nعَسٰى رَبُّهٗۤ اِنْ طَلَّقَكُنَّ اَنْ يُّبْدِلَهٗۤ اَزْوَاجًا خَيْرًا مِّنْكُنَّ مُسْلِمٰتٍ مُّؤْمِنٰتٍ قٰنِتٰتٍ تٰٓئِبٰتٍ عٰبِدٰتٍ سٰٓئِحٰتٍ ثَيِّبٰتٍ وَّاَبْكَارًا‏(5)\nA’SAA RABBOHU IN TALLAQAKUNNA AN YYUBDELAH AZWAAJANW KHAYRAN MMENKUNNA MUSLEMAATIN MMUMENAATIN QAANETAATIN TAAAEBAATIN A’AABEDAATIN SAAAEHAATIN SAYBAATIN WWAABKAARAN.\nIt may be, if he divorced you (all), that Allah will give him in exchange consorts better than you, who submit (their wills), who believe, who are devout, who turn to Allah in repentance, who worship (in humility), who travel (for Faith) and fast, previously married or virgins. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا قُوْۤا اَنْفُسَكُمْ وَاَهْلِيْكُمْ نَارًا وَّقُوْدُهَا النَّاسُ وَالْحِجَارَةُ عَلَيْهَا مَلٰٓئِكَةٌ غِلَاظٌ شِدَادٌ لَّا يَعْصُوْنَ اللّٰهَ مَاۤ اَمَرَهُمْ وَيَفْعَلُوْنَ مَا يُؤْمَرُوْنَ‏(6)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO QOOA ANFOSAKUM WAAHLEEKUM NAARAN WWAQOODUHAA NAASO WAL HEJAARAH A’LAYHAA MALAAAEKATUN GHELAAZUN SHEDAADUN LAA YAA’SOONA LAAHA MAA AAMARAHUM WA YAF-A’LOON MAA YUMAROONA.\nO ye who believe! save yourselves and your families from a Fire whose fuel is Men and Stones, over which are (appointed) angels stern (and) severe, who flinch not (from executing) the Commands they receive from Allah, but do (precisely) what they are commanded. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لَا تَعْتَذِرُوا الْيَوْمَ‌ؕ اِنَّمَا تُجْزَوْنَ مَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(7)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA KAFAROO LAA TAA’TAZEROOA AL-YAWMA INNAMAA TUJZAWNA MAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\n(They will say), “O ye Unbelievers! Make no excuses this Day! Ye are being but requited for all that ye did!” \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا تُوْبُوْۤا اِلَى اللّٰهِ تَوْبَةً نَّصُوْحًا ؕ عَسٰى رَبُّكُمْ اَنْ يُّكَفِّرَ عَنْكُمْ سَيِّاٰتِكُمْ وَيُدْخِلَكُمْ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ ۙ يَوْمَ لَا يُخْزِى اللّٰهُ النَّبِىَّ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مَعَهٗ‌ ۚ نُوْرُهُمْ يَسْعٰى بَيْنَ اَيْدِيْهِمْ وَبِاَيْمَانِهِمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ رَبَّنَاۤ اَ تْمِمْ لَنَا نُوْرَنَا وَاغْفِرْ لَنَا‌ ۚ اِنَّكَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(8)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO TOOBOOA ELAL LAAHE TAWBATAN NNASOOHAN A’SAA RABBOKUM AN YYUKAFFERA A’NKUM SAYAAATEKUM WAYUDKHELAKUM JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO YAWMA LAA YUKHZEAA LAAHO NABIYYA WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO MA-A’HU NOORUHUM YAS-A’A BAYNA AYDEEHIM WABEAAYMAANEHEM YAQOOLOONA RABBANAA AATMEM LANAA NOORANAA FIRLANAA LANAA INNAKA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nO ye who believe! Turn to Allah with sincere repentance: In the hope that your Lord will remove from you your ills and admit you to Gardens beneath which Rivers flow, the Day that Allah will not permit to be humiliated the Prophet and those who believe with him. Their Light will run forward before them and by their right hands, while they say, “Our Lord! Perfect our Light for us, and grant us Forgiveness: for Thou hast power over all things.” \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّبِىُّ جَاهِدِ الْكُفَّارَ وَالْمُنٰفِقِيْنَ وَاغْلُظْ عَلَيْهِمْ‌ؕ وَمَاْوٰٮهُمْ جَهَنَّمُ‌ؕ وَبِئْسَ الْمَصِيْرُ‏(9)\nYAA AYYOHAL NABIYYO JAAHEDE KUFFAARA KAAFEREENA WAAGHLUZ WA WAMAAWAAHUM JAHANNAM WA WA BEASAL MASEER.\nO Prophet! Strive hard against the Unbelievers and the Hypocrites, and be firm against them. Their abode is Hell, an evil refuge (indeed). \nضَرَبَ اللّٰهُ مَثَلًا لِّلَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوا امْرَاَتَ نُوْحٍ وَّ امْرَاَتَ لُوْطٍ‌ ؕ كَانَتَا تَحْتَ عَبْدَيْنِ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا صَالِحَيْنِ فَخَانَتٰهُمَا فَلَمْ يُغْنِيَا عَنْهُمَا مِنَ اللّٰهِ شَيْئًا وَّقِيْلَ ادْخُلَا النَّارَ مَعَ الدّٰخِلِيْنَ‏(10)\nZARABA LAAHO MASALAA LIL-LAZEENA KAFARUL AMRAATA NOOHIN WA AMRAATA LOOTIM KAANATAA TAHTA A’ABDAYNE MIN E’EBAADENAA SAALEHAYNE FAKHAANATAAHUMAA FALAM YUGHNEEA A’ANHUMAA MENAL LAAHE SHAY-ANW WWAQEELA ADKHULAA NAARAL LAAHA AD-DAAKHELEENA.\nAllah sets forth, for an example to the Unbelievers, the wife of Noah and the wife of Lut: they were (respectively) under two of our righteous servants, but they were false to their (husbands), and they profited nothing before Allah on their account, but were told: “Enter ye the Fire along with (others) that enter!” \nوَضَرَبَ اللّٰهُ مَثَلًا لِّلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا امْرَاَتَ فِرْعَوْنَ‌ۘ اِذْ قَالَتْ رَبِّ ابْنِ لِىْ عِنْدَكَ بَيْتًا فِى الْجَنَّةِ وَنَجِّنِىْ مِنْ فِرْعَوْنَ وَعَمَلِهٖ وَنَجِّنِىْ مِنَ الْقَوْمِ الظّٰلِمِيْنَۙ‏(11)\nWA ZARABA LAAHO MASALAA LIL-LAZEENA AAMANOO AMRAATA FIR-A’WNA IZ QAALAT RABBE MARYAM LEE E’ENDAKA BAYTAN FIL JANNAH WA NAJJENEE MIN FIR-A’WNA WAA’AMALEH WA NAJJENEE MENAL QAWMIL ZAALEMEEN.\nAnd Allah sets forth, as an example to those who believe the wife of Pharaoh: Behold she said: “O my Lord! Build for me, in nearness to Thee, a mansion in the Garden, and save me from Pharaoh and his doings, and save me from those that do wrong”; \nوَمَرْيَمَ ابْنَتَ عِمْرٰنَ الَّتِىْۤ اَحْصَنَتْ فَرْجَهَا فَنَفَخْنَا فِيْهِ مِنْ رُّوْحِنَا وَصَدَّقَتْ بِكَلِمٰتِ رَبِّهَا وَكُتُبِهٖ وَكَانَتْ مِنَ الْقٰنِتِيْنَ‏(12)\nWA MARYAMAL ABNATA E’EMRAANA LATEE AAHSANAT FARJAHAA FANAFAKHNAA FEEHE MIN RROOHENAA WASADDAQAT BEKALEMAATE RABBEHAA WA KOTOBEHI WA KAANAT MENAL AL-QAANETEENA.\nAnd Mary the daughter of 'Imran, who guarded her chastity; and We breathed into (her body) of Our spirit; and she testified to the truth of the words of her Lord and of His Revelations, and was one of the devout (servants).",
  "merits": "Surah al-Tahreem (The Prohibition)\nThis ‘Madani’ Surah has 12 verses. It is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that the one who recites this Surah will be from those who always seek sincere repentance from Allah (s.w.t.). The recitation of this Surah and drinking of its water acts as a cure from many ailments and diseases.\nIf this Surah is recited by a person who is not getting sleep then he will be able to sleep and if recited by a person who is frightened, he will become calm. Frequent recitation also helps a person who is in debt to clear his debts."
}
